 [; #1051 — this case reads the child environment with the `echo` BUILTIN,
    and every hermetic case must. §4.2 is explicit that `env-clear=true`
    hands the child EXACTLY the declared set, so the child has no `PATH`;
    a stage body that shells out to `printenv` is then asking the CHILD
    SHELL to resolve an external command with nothing to resolve it
    against, and what happens next belongs to whichever `sh` §4.1
    resolved from the PARENT's PATH — not to cx. Measured both ways on
    one binary: macOS /bin/sh substitutes a default PATH of
    `/usr/gnu/bin:/usr/local/bin:/bin:/usr/bin:.` and finds printenv
    (green), while the nix bash the devbox/make PATH puts first
    substitutes `/no-such-path` and does not (exit 127, `printenv:
    command not found` on stderr, stdout EMPTY). Same binary, same
    fixture, opposite verdicts — which is exactly how this read as a
    "deterministic under the runner, green standalone" impl bug for two
    grading passes. A builtin needs no PATH, so the case now grades the
    RULED CO-15 layering and nothing else. Its siblings 065/066 keep
    `printenv` legitimately: they run under §4.2's augment default, where
    the child inherits PATH. ]

