 [; §4.1's argv[0] resolution against the CHILD's PATH (#1052). §4.1:
    "resolved against `PATH` (the child's when `$env` overrides it, else
    the parent's)". The pronoun is `PATH`, so the child's PATH governs
    exactly when an `$env` LAYER NAMES the key — which is why the granted
    hermetic cases above (050 / 051 / 067) still resolve `env` on the
    PARENT's PATH: `env-clear=true` alone names nothing. That is coherent
    rather than a contradiction — resolution yields an ABSOLUTE path and
    the child execs that, so a child with no PATH never needed one to
    start; §4.1 is describing where the PARENT's resolver looks.

    proc_resolve_exec took no environment at all before this and always
    called os.find_abs_path_of_executable — i.e. always the PARENT's
    PATH — so the first half of that clause was unimplemented and no
    fixture named the cell. Measured on the pre-fix binary: 085 / 089 /
    090 / 091 were CXER4001 / CXER4005 (the stub is on no parent PATH),
    and 087 was GREEN with `stdout='hi\n'` — the same bug seen from the
    other side, since a child PATH naming nothing must find nothing.
    086 and 088 are the negatives and were green pre-fix; they pin that
    this changed only the cell it was supposed to.

    Hermetic per the #1051 lesson: the stub dir is named by ABSOLUTE
    path, the stub is `/bin/echo` behind a symlink, and no child shell is
    ever asked to resolve anything against a PATH it does not have. ]

 [case id=process-085-run-argv0-resolves-against-child-path level=core gate=enforced grant='subprocess read write'
  [tags process run env search-path resolution child-path granted effort-b]
  [in-cx [#
[empty]
#]]
  [in-code [#
[?lib 'cx-stdlib/process']
[?lib 'cx-stdlib/io']
[?lib 'cx-stdlib/strings']
[?if [$io:exists "/tmp/cx-conf-1052-bin"] [then [$io:remove-tree "/tmp/cx-conf-1052-bin"]]]
[$io:make-dirs "/tmp/cx-conf-1052-bin"]
[$io:symlink "/bin/echo" "/tmp/cx-conf-1052-bin/cxstub1052"]
[?let [= $r [$process:run ("cxstub1052", "STUB-HIT") env=[map PATH="/tmp/cx-conf-1052-bin"]]] [$strings:trim $r@stdout]]
#]]
  [out-text [#
'STUB-HIT'
#]]
 ]

